// Partitions (docs/indexes.md, section 5.4): how many have each value,
// the values that have any, and what a `for ... where x.f == v` (or of
// any of some values, or of none of them) visits, are as without the
// indexes, as the entities change their values, come and go; on one core
// and on many. Kept as a set for each value, the `for`s it answers go
// through its bits (via_partition, in_set); where no system changes the
// field and rows move anyway, it keeps the archetype's rows by its values
// (clustered).
// RUN: sed -e '/\/\/I$/d' -e 's|^\( *\)//P |\1|' %S/Inputs/partition.ent > %t.plain.ent
// RUN: %ent run %t.plain.ent > %t.plain
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/partition.ent 2>&1 > %t.one | count 0
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.plain
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/partition.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/partition.ent -I %S/../../devices \
// RUN:   | ent-opt --ent-indexes | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VIA
// RUN: sed -e '/\/\/I$/d' %S/Inputs/partition_kept.ent > %t.kept_plain.ent
// RUN: %ent run %t.kept_plain.ent > %t.kept_plain
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/partition_kept.ent 2>&1 > %t.kept | count 0
// RUN: cmp %t.kept %t.kept_plain
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/partition_kept.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.kept_all
// RUN: cmp %t.kept %t.kept_all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=KEPT --input-file=%t.kept
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/partition_kept.ent -I %S/../../devices \
// RUN:   | ent-opt --ent-indexes | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLUSTERED

